module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Extension.Generators
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Kaehler.Basic
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.Cotangent.LichtenbaumSchlessinger
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Kaehler.Presentation

/-!
# Functoriality of the Lichtenbaum--Schlessinger complex

Let `A → B`, `A' → B'`, `A → A'`, `B → B'` be a commutative square of ring maps, let `P → B` be a
polynomial presentation of `B` over `A` with chosen generators `f_t`, `t ∈ T`, of its defining
ideal, and let `P' → B'` be a polynomial presentation of `B'` over `A'` whose chosen generators
are indexed by `T' = T ⊔ S` and which, over `T`, are the images `f'_t` of the `f_t` along a map
`P → P'` of polynomial algebras lying over `A → A'` and `B → B'`. These data induce a map from
the Lichtenbaum--Schlessinger complex

`L  : Rel/TrivRel → F ⊗_P B → Ω_{P/A} ⊗_P B`

of the first presentation to that of the second,

`L' : Rel'/TrivRel' → F' ⊗_{P'} B' → Ω_{P'/A'} ⊗_{P'} B'`,

where `F = ⨁_{t ∈ T} P` and `F' = ⨁_{t' ∈ T'} P'`, `Rel` and `Rel'` are the kernels of the maps
`F → P` and `F' → P'` given by multiplication by the chosen generators on the coordinates, and
`TrivRel ⊆ Rel`, `TrivRel' ⊆ Rel'` are generated by the Koszul relations.

## Main definitions

* `Algebra.Presentation.LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom`: the choices, namely a map `P → P'` of
  polynomial algebras over the square together with the requirement that the generator of the
  defining ideal of `P' → B'` indexed by `t ∈ T` be the image of the one indexed by `t`.
* `Algebra.Presentation.LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom.freeMap`: the map `F → F'` placing the
  coordinates of `F` at the indices `T ⊆ T'`, an instance of
  `Stacks.KaehlerDifferential.Presentation.freeMapₛₗ`.
* `Algebra.Presentation.LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom.relationQuotientMap`: the vertical arrow
  `Rel/TrivRel → Rel'/TrivRel'` in degree `-2`.
* `Algebra.Presentation.LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom.freeTensorMap`: the vertical arrow
  `F ⊗_P B → F' ⊗_{P'} B'` in degree `-1`.
* `Algebra.Presentation.LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom.differentialTensorMap`: the vertical arrow
  `Ω_{P/A} ⊗_P B → Ω_{P'/A'} ⊗_{P'} B'` in degree `0`.

## Main results

* `Algebra.Presentation.LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom.freeTensorMap_relationBoundaryR`: the square
  formed by the two arrows `Rel/TrivRel → F ⊗_P B`, `Rel'/TrivRel' → F' ⊗_{P'} B'` and the
  vertical arrows in degrees `-2` and `-1` commutes.
* `Algebra.Presentation.LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom.differentialTensorMap_relationDifferentialB`:
  the square formed by the two arrows `F ⊗_P B → Ω_{P/A} ⊗_P B`,
  `F' ⊗_{P'} B' → Ω_{P'/A'} ⊗_{P'} B'` and the vertical arrows in degrees `-1` and `0`
  commutes.
* `Algebra.Presentation.LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom.relationQuotientMap_smul`: the arrow in
  degree `-2` is semilinear over `B → B'` for the descended module structures, as the arrows in
  degrees `-1` and `0` are by construction.

## Implementation notes

The terms of `L` are taken in the spelling of `StacksFrontier.Cotangent.LichtenbaumSchlessinger`,
namely `Algebra.Presentation.relationQuotient`, `B ⊗[P.Ring] (T →₀ P.Ring)` and
`B ⊗[P.Ring] Ω[P.Ring⁄A]`, and the two horizontal arrows are
`Algebra.Presentation.relationBoundaryR` and `Algebra.Presentation.relationDifferentialB`.

The target of a vertical arrow is a module over `B'` and its source a module over `B`, so the
arrows in degrees `-1` and `0` are stated as `B`-linear maps, which is possible because the
scalars of a tensor product over `P'` with `B'` on the left restrict along `B → B'`. The arrow in
degree `-2` is instead built as a semilinear map over `P → P'`, the ring over which the relation
modules are defined before any descent, and its semilinearity over `B → B'` for the descended
structures of `Algebra.Presentation.relationModule` is recorded separately.

The index type of the generators of the defining ideal of the second presentation is literally
`T ⊕ S`, which is how the source writes `T' = T ⊔ S`: the generators indexed by `T` are the
images of the old ones, and those indexed by `S` are the extra ones needed because the image of
the defining ideal of `P → B` need not generate that of `P' → B'`.

The second diagram displayed in the source, which compares the above with the canonical maps
`L_{B/A} → L` and `L_{B'/A'} → L'` of Tag 09CG, is
`LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom.canonicalCotangentToLichtenbaumSchlessinger_naturality` in
the namespace `Algebra.Presentation`, in the module
`StacksFrontier.Cotangent.LichtenbaumSchlessingerComparisonNatural`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09D7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09D7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09CD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09CD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09CG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09CG)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open KaehlerDifferential TensorProduct

universe u₀ v₀ u u' v v' w

namespace Algebra.Presentation

attribute [local instance] SMulCommClass.of_commMonoid

section Single

variable {R : Type u₀} {Sr : Type v₀} {ι τ : Type w} [CommRing R] [CommRing Sr] [Algebra R Sr]

/-- The map `F → P` sends `p` times the basis vector of an equation to `p` times that
equation. -/
lemma relationMap_single (Q : Presentation R Sr ι τ) (t : τ) (p : Q.Ring) :
    relationMap Q (Finsupp.single t p) = p * Q.relation t := by
  rw [relationMap, Finsupp.lsum_single]
  rfl

/-- The map `F → Ω_{P/R}` sends `p` times the basis vector of an equation to `p` times the
differential of that equation. -/
lemma relationDifferential_single (Q : Presentation R Sr ι τ) (t : τ) (p : Q.Ring) :
    relationDifferential Q (Finsupp.single t p) = p • D R Q.Ring (Q.relation t) := by
  rw [relationDifferential, Finsupp.lsum_single]
  rfl

end Single

variable {A : Type u} {A' : Type u'} {B : Type v} {B' : Type v'}
  [CommRing A] [CommRing A'] [CommRing B] [CommRing B']
  [Algebra A B] [Algebra A' B'] [Algebra A A'] [Algebra B B']
  {X X' T S : Type w}

/-- The choices entering the functoriality of the Lichtenbaum--Schlessinger complex: a map
`P → P'` of the polynomial algebras of two presentations lying over a commutative square of ring
maps, such that the generator of the defining ideal of `P' → B'` indexed by `t ∈ T` is the image
of the generator indexed by `t`. The remaining generators, indexed by `S`, are unconstrained. -/
structure LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom (P : Presentation A B X T)
    (P' : Presentation A' B' X' (T ⊕ S)) where
  /-- The map `P → P'` of polynomial algebras over the square. -/
  toHom : Generators.Hom P.toGenerators P'.toGenerators
  /-- The generator `f'_t` of the defining ideal of `P' → B'` is the image of `f_t`. -/
  relation_inl : ∀ t : T, P'.relation (Sum.inl t) = toHom.toAlgHom (P.relation t)

namespace LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom

variable {P : Presentation A B X T} {P' : Presentation A' B' X' (T ⊕ S)}
  (f : LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom P P')

/-- The map `P → P'` as a ring homomorphism. -/
abbrev ringHom : P.Ring →+* P'.Ring := f.toHom.toAlgHom.toRingHom

/-- The generator `f'_t` is the image of `f_t`. -/
lemma relation_inl_ringHom (t : T) : P'.relation (Sum.inl t) = f.ringHom (P.relation t) :=
  f.relation_inl t

/-- The map `F = ⨁_{t ∈ T} P → F' = ⨁_{t' ∈ T'} P'` given by `P → P'` on the coordinates
indexed by `T ⊆ T'` and by zero on the remaining ones. -/
def freeMap : (T →₀ P.Ring) →ₛₗ[f.ringHom] ((T ⊕ S) →₀ P'.Ring) :=
  Stacks.KaehlerDifferential.Presentation.freeMapₛₗ f.ringHom Sum.inl

/-- The map `F → F'` sends the basis vector at `t ∈ T` with coefficient `p` to the basis vector at
`t ∈ T'` with coefficient the image of `p` in `P'`. -/
@[simp]
lemma freeMap_single (t : T) (p : P.Ring) :
    f.freeMap (Finsupp.single t p) = Finsupp.single (Sum.inl t) (f.ringHom p) :=
  Stacks.KaehlerDifferential.Presentation.freeMapₛₗ_single _ _ _ _

/-- The map `F → F'` is compatible with the multiplication maps `F → P` and `F' → P'`. -/
lemma relationMap_freeMap (x : T →₀ P.Ring) :
    relationMap P' (f.freeMap x) = f.ringHom (relationMap P x) := by
  induction x using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp only [map_zero]
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, hx, hy]
  | single t p =>
      rw [f.freeMap_single, relationMap_single, relationMap_single,
        f.relation_inl_ringHom t, map_mul]

/-- The map `Rel → Rel'` induced by `F → F'`. -/
def relationsMap : relations P →ₛₗ[f.ringHom] relations P' :=
  (f.freeMap.domRestrict (relations P)).codRestrict (relations P') fun r ↦ by
    have hr : relationMap P (r : T →₀ P.Ring) = 0 := LinearMap.mem_ker.1 r.2
    refine LinearMap.mem_ker.2 ?_
    change relationMap P' (f.freeMap (r : T →₀ P.Ring)) = 0
    rw [f.relationMap_freeMap, hr, map_zero]

/-- The map `Rel → Rel'` is the restriction of `F → F'`. -/
@[simp]
lemma relationsMap_coe (r : relations P) :
    (f.relationsMap r : (T ⊕ S) →₀ P'.Ring) = f.freeMap (r : T →₀ P.Ring) := rfl

/-- The map `F → F'` carries the Koszul relation attached to `s, t ∈ T` to the one attached to
the corresponding pair of indices in `T'`. -/
lemma freeMap_trivialRelation (s t : T) :
    f.freeMap (trivialRelation P s t) = trivialRelation P' (Sum.inl s) (Sum.inl t) := by
  rw [trivialRelation, map_sub, f.freeMap_single, f.freeMap_single, trivialRelation,
    ← f.relation_inl_ringHom s, ← f.relation_inl_ringHom t]

/-- The map `Rel → Rel'` carries the Koszul relation attached to `s, t ∈ T` to the one attached
to the corresponding pair of indices in `T'`. -/
lemma relationsMap_trivialRelationInRelations (s t : T) :
    f.relationsMap (trivialRelationInRelations P s t) =
      trivialRelationInRelations P' (Sum.inl s) (Sum.inl t) :=
  Subtype.ext (by rw [f.relationsMap_coe]; exact f.freeMap_trivialRelation s t)

/-- The map `Rel → Rel'` carries `TrivRel` into `TrivRel'`. -/
lemma trivialRelations_le_comap :
    trivialRelations P ≤ (trivialRelations P').comap f.relationsMap := by
  rw [trivialRelations, Submodule.span_le]
  rintro x ⟨⟨s, t⟩, rfl⟩
  refine Submodule.mem_comap.2 ?_
  rw [f.relationsMap_trivialRelationInRelations]
  exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨(Sum.inl s, Sum.inl t), rfl⟩

/-- The map `Rel/TrivRel → Rel'/TrivRel'` induced by `Rel → Rel'`, in degree `-2`. -/
@[stacks 09D7 "the vertical arrow Rel/TrivRel → Rel'/TrivRel' of the displayed diagram"]
def relationQuotientMap : relationQuotient P →ₛₗ[f.ringHom] relationQuotient P' :=
  Submodule.mapQ _ _ f.relationsMap f.trivialRelations_le_comap

/-- The map `Rel/TrivRel → Rel'/TrivRel'` sends the class of `r` to the class of its image in
`Rel'`. -/
@[simp]
lemma relationQuotientMap_mk (r : relations P) :
    f.relationQuotientMap (Submodule.Quotient.mk r) =
      Submodule.Quotient.mk (f.relationsMap r) := rfl

section Square

variable [Algebra A B'] [IsScalarTower A A' B'] [IsScalarTower A B B']

/-- Compatibility of `P → P'` with the two augmentations and with `B → B'`. -/
lemma algebraMap_ringHom (p : P.Ring) :
    algebraMap P'.Ring B' (f.ringHom p) = algebraMap B B' (algebraMap P.Ring B p) := by
  rw [P.algebraMap_apply, P'.algebraMap_apply]
  exact f.toHom.algebraMap_toAlgHom p

/-- The arrow in degree `-2` is semilinear over `B → B'` for the module structures obtained by
descending the actions on `Rel/TrivRel` and `Rel'/TrivRel'` along `P → B` and `P' → B'`. -/
lemma relationQuotientMap_smul (b : B) (q : relationQuotient P) :
    letI := relationModule P
    letI := relationModule P'
    f.relationQuotientMap (b • q) = algebraMap B B' b • f.relationQuotientMap q := by
  let _ := relationModule P
  let _ := relationModule P'
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ := P.algebraMap_surjective b
  rw [relationModule_smul P p q, map_smulₛₗ, ← f.algebraMap_ringHom p,
    relationModule_smul P' (f.ringHom p)]

/-- Scalar multiplication by `b : B` on `1 ⊗ m` in `B' ⊗ M` is the tensor with the image of `b`. -/
private theorem smul_one_tmul_eq {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    [Algebra R B'] (b : B) (m : M) :
    b • ((1 : B') ⊗ₜ[R] m) = algebraMap B B' b ⊗ₜ[R] m := by
  rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', Algebra.smul_def, mul_one]

/-- **Stacks 09D7.** The arrow `F ⊗_P B → F' ⊗_{P'} B'` of the diagram, in degree `-1`. -/
@[stacks 09D7 "the vertical arrow F ⊗_P B → F' ⊗_{P'} B' of the displayed diagram"]
def freeTensorMap :
    (B ⊗[P.Ring] (T →₀ P.Ring)) →ₗ[B] B' ⊗[P'.Ring] ((T ⊕ S) →₀ P'.Ring) := by
  letI := ((algebraMap B B').comp (algebraMap P.Ring B)).toAlgebra
  haveI : IsScalarTower P.Ring B B' := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  letI := f.toHom.toAlgHom.toAlgebra
  haveI : IsScalarTower P.Ring P'.Ring B' :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x ↦ (f.algebraMap_ringHom x).symm
  refine LinearMap.liftBaseChange B ?_
  refine (TensorProduct.mk P'.Ring B' ((T ⊕ S) →₀ P'.Ring) 1).restrictScalars P.Ring ∘ₗ ?_
  exact { toFun := f.freeMap
          map_add' := f.freeMap.map_add
          map_smul' := fun p x ↦ f.freeMap.map_smulₛₗ p x }

/-- The arrow in degree `-1` sends `b ⊗ x` to the image of `b` tensor the image of `x`. -/
@[simp]
lemma freeTensorMap_tmul (b : B) (x : T →₀ P.Ring) :
    f.freeTensorMap (b ⊗ₜ[P.Ring] x) = algebraMap B B' b ⊗ₜ[P'.Ring] f.freeMap x := by
  rw [freeTensorMap, LinearMap.liftBaseChange_tmul, LinearMap.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply,
    LinearMap.restrictScalars_apply, TensorProduct.mk_apply]
  exact smul_one_tmul_eq _ _

/-- **Stacks 09D7.** The arrow `Ω_{P/A} ⊗_P B → Ω_{P'/A'} ⊗_{P'} B'` of the diagram, in degree
`0`. -/
@[stacks 09D7 "the vertical arrow Ω_{P/A} ⊗_P B → Ω_{P'/A'} ⊗_{P'} B' of the displayed diagram"]
def differentialTensorMap :
    (B ⊗[P.Ring] Ω[P.Ring⁄A]) →ₗ[B] B' ⊗[P'.Ring] Ω[P'.Ring⁄A'] := by
  letI := ((algebraMap B B').comp (algebraMap P.Ring B)).toAlgebra
  haveI : IsScalarTower P.Ring B B' := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' rfl
  letI := f.toHom.toAlgHom.toAlgebra
  haveI : IsScalarTower P.Ring P'.Ring B' :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x ↦ (f.algebraMap_ringHom x).symm
  haveI : IsScalarTower A P.Ring P'.Ring :=
    IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq fun x ↦ (f.toHom.toAlgHom.commutes x).symm
  refine LinearMap.liftBaseChange B ?_
  exact (TensorProduct.mk P'.Ring B' Ω[P'.Ring⁄A'] 1).restrictScalars P.Ring ∘ₗ
    KaehlerDifferential.map A A' P.Ring P'.Ring

/-- The arrow in degree `0` sends `b ⊗ d p` to the image of `b` tensor `d` of the image of
`p`. -/
@[simp]
lemma differentialTensorMap_tmul_D (b : B) (p : P.Ring) :
    f.differentialTensorMap (b ⊗ₜ[P.Ring] D A P.Ring p) =
      algebraMap B B' b ⊗ₜ[P'.Ring] D A' P'.Ring (f.ringHom p) := by
  rw [differentialTensorMap, LinearMap.liftBaseChange_tmul, LinearMap.coe_comp,
    Function.comp_apply, KaehlerDifferential.map_D, LinearMap.restrictScalars_apply,
    TensorProduct.mk_apply]
  exact smul_one_tmul_eq _ _

/-- The arrow `Rel/TrivRel → F ⊗_P B` of `L` followed by the vertical arrow in degree `-1`
agrees, on the class of a relation, with the vertical arrow in degree `-2` followed by
`Rel'/TrivRel' → F' ⊗_{P'} B'`. -/
lemma freeTensorMap_relationBoundaryR_mk (r : relations P) :
    f.freeTensorMap (relationBoundaryR P (Submodule.Quotient.mk r)) =
      relationBoundaryR P' (f.relationQuotientMap (Submodule.Quotient.mk r)) := by
  rw [f.relationQuotientMap_mk]
  erw [relationBoundaryR_mk, relationBoundaryR_mk]
  rw [f.freeTensorMap_tmul, map_one, f.relationsMap_coe]

/-- **Stacks 09D7.** The left-hand square of the displayed diagram commutes: the arrow
`Rel/TrivRel → F ⊗_P B` followed by the vertical arrow in degree `-1` agrees with the vertical
arrow in degree `-2` followed by `Rel'/TrivRel' → F' ⊗_{P'} B'`. -/
@[stacks 09D7 "commutativity of the left-hand square of the displayed diagram"]
lemma freeTensorMap_relationBoundaryR (q : relationQuotient P) :
    f.freeTensorMap (relationBoundaryR P q) =
      relationBoundaryR P' (f.relationQuotientMap q) :=
  Quotient.inductionOn q fun r ↦ f.freeTensorMap_relationBoundaryR_mk r

/-- The arrow in degree `0` applied to `b` tensor the differential of a formal combination of
the equations. -/
lemma differentialTensorMap_tmul_relationDifferential (b : B) (x : T →₀ P.Ring) :
    f.differentialTensorMap (b ⊗ₜ[P.Ring] relationDifferential P x) =
      algebraMap B B' b ⊗ₜ[P'.Ring] relationDifferential P' (f.freeMap x) := by
  induction x using Finsupp.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp only [map_zero, TensorProduct.tmul_zero]
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, TensorProduct.tmul_add, hx, hy]
  | single t p =>
      rw [f.freeMap_single, relationDifferential_single, relationDifferential_single,
        ← TensorProduct.smul_tmul, f.differentialTensorMap_tmul_D,
        ← TensorProduct.smul_tmul, f.relation_inl_ringHom t, Algebra.smul_def,
        Algebra.smul_def, f.algebraMap_ringHom p, map_mul]

/-- **Stacks 09D7.** The right-hand square of the displayed diagram commutes: the arrow
`F ⊗_P B → Ω_{P/A} ⊗_P B` followed by the vertical arrow in degree `0` agrees with the vertical
arrow in degree `-1` followed by `F' ⊗_{P'} B' → Ω_{P'/A'} ⊗_{P'} B'`. -/
@[stacks 09D7 "commutativity of the right-hand square of the displayed diagram"]
lemma differentialTensorMap_relationDifferentialB (z : B ⊗[P.Ring] (T →₀ P.Ring)) :
    f.differentialTensorMap (relationDifferentialB P z) =
      relationDifferentialB P' (f.freeTensorMap z) := by
  induction z using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, hx, hy]
  | tmul b x =>
      rw [relationDifferentialB_tmul, f.freeTensorMap_tmul, relationDifferentialB_tmul,
        f.differentialTensorMap_tmul_relationDifferential]

end Square

end LichtenbaumSchlessingerHom

end Algebra.Presentation

end
